{%- comment -%} 2 · CITIES (tint). Seven chips over one map. The app follows your location, so
     there is no switcher. {%- endcomment %}
<section class="mt-section mt-section--tint" id="cities" aria-labelledby="cities-title">
  <div class="mt-section__inner">
    <header class="mt-header mt-header--center">
      <p class="mt-eyebrow">Seven Cities</p>
      <h2 class="mt-header__title" id="cities-title">Every Line. Even the Ones Still Being Built.</h2>
      <p class="mt-header__sub">InTransit opens on the city you’re in, with every running and under-construction line, so a new line is ready the day it opens. Pan the map to look around any other city.</p>
    </header>
    <ul class="mt-chips" role="list">
      <li>Ahmedabad</li>
      <li>Bengaluru</li>
      <li>Chennai</li>
      <li>Kolkata</li>
      <li>Mumbai</li>
      <li>New Delhi</li>
      <li>Pune</li>
    </ul>
    {% render "shot.html", name: "cities-map", dark: true, width: 1200, height: 675, sizes: "min(calc(100vw - 3rem), 1200px)", alt: "The metro map of InTransit", class: "mt-wide-shot" %}
    <p class="mt-header__note mt-centred-note">Your city next? <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=A%20city%20for%20InTransit">Tell Nikhil which one.</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} 3 · LIVE ACTIVITIES (dark). One picture: the `live-activities` artboard
     (1200 x 675 at 1x). The band is dark in both appearances, so the picture has no dark
     version. {%- endcomment %}
<section class="mt-section mt-section--dark" id="live-activities" aria-labelledby="live-activities-title">
  <div class="mt-section__inner">
    <header class="mt-header mt-header--center">
      <p class="mt-eyebrow">Live Activities</p>
      <h2 class="mt-header__title" id="live-activities-title">Never Miss Your Stop</h2>
      <p class="mt-header__sub">Your next station, your interchange and your arrival time stay on the Lock Screen and in the Dynamic Island. When your stop comes up, InTransit lets you know with a notification and a tap you can feel.</p>
    </header>
    {% render "shot.html", name: "live-activities", width: 1200, height: 675, sizes: "min(calc(100vw - 3rem), 1200px)", alt: "Live Activities of InTransit on the Lock Screen and in the Dynamic Island", class: "mt-wide-shot" %}
    <p class="mt-header__note mt-centred-note">The colours blend from the line you board to the line you leave on. On Apple Watch too, in the Smart Stack.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} 4 · UNDERGROUND (plain). A split with a phone. {%- endcomment %}
<section class="mt-section" id="underground" aria-labelledby="underground-title">
  <div class="mt-section__inner mt-split">
    <header class="mt-header">
      <p class="mt-eyebrow">Underground</p>
      <h2 class="mt-header__title" id="underground-title">Still on Track When the Signal Drops</h2>
      <p class="mt-header__sub">Deep in a tunnel, most apps lose you. InTransit keeps counting the stations, and shows its best guess on the map with a dashed ring until the signal is back.</p>
      <p class="mt-header__note">Maps and routes live on your iPhone, so they work with no signal at all.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="mt-split__media mt-shot-phone">
      {% render "shot.html", name: "underground-phone", dark: true, width: 256, height: 523, sizes: "min(16rem, calc(100vw - 3rem))", alt: "InTransit on iPhone with no signal, still showing the route and the next station" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

